<title>SINGAPORE: City Developments 1996 net up 33.8 pct.</title>
<headline>City Developments 1996 net up 33.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996 (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   535.42  vs  400.16</p>
<p>    First/final dividend (pct)	15.00  vs   15.00</p>
<p>    Special dividend (pct)	     5.00  vs    nil</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)		   68.04  vs   51.43</p>
<p>    Group share fully diluted (cts) 67.35  vs   50.46</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)		  2.64  vs    1.97</p>
<p>    Investment income		    7.87  vs    6.28</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest     44.04  vs   35.61</p>
<p>    Interest expense		   147.70  vs   89.00</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	141.46  vs   95.47</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     839.06  vs  612.25</p>
<p>    Income from associates	    23.01  vs   29.07</p>
<p>    Tax				    246.44  vs  184.48</p>
<p>    Minorities (gain)		   80.21  vs   56.67</p>
<p>    Extraordinary gain		  26.74  vs    nil</p>
<p>Note - City Developments Ltd is a property developer with hotel interests.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
